[00:22.15] I am born
[00:26.85] I am me
[00:29.83] I am new
[00:34.68] I am free
[00:36.80] 
[00:42.94] Look at me
[00:47.89] I am young
[00:50.62] Sight unseen
[00:55.74] Life unsung
[00:59.20] 
[01:58.88] My eyes have just been opened and they're open very wide
[02:03.25] Images around me don't identify inside
[02:07.03] Just one blur I recognize, the one that soothes and feeds
[02:11.33] My way of life is easy and as simple are my needs
[02:16.63] 
[02:27.69] Yet my eyes are drawn toward the mountain in the east
[02:32.35] Fascinates and captivates, gives my heart no peace
[02:37.16] The mountain holds the sunrise in the prison of the night
[02:42.17] Until bursting forth from rocky chains, the valley floods with light
[03:09.22] Living one long sunrise, for to me, all things are new
[03:13.11] I've never watched the sky grow pale, or strolled through fields of dew
[03:17.21] I do not know of dust to dust, I live from breath to breath
[03:21.54] I live to climb that mountain to the Fountain of Lamneth
[03:26.12] 
[03:37.56] Yet my eyes are drawn toward the mountain in the east
[03:42.52] Fascinates and captivates and gives my heart no peace
[03:47.12] The mountain holds the sunrise in the prison of the night
[03:51.93] Until bursting forth from rocky chains, the valley floods with light
